    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Each turn all players simultaneously choose one card and reveal them together. Cards are placed in ascending order onto one of four table rows: each card goes on the row whose end card is lower than the played card and closest in value (smallest difference). If a card is the 6th on a row, the player takes the five existing cards as penalty (Horns) and their card starts a new row. If the played card is lower than all row ends, the player chooses a row to take and their card starts that row. After 10 turns the round ends; players sum their Horn points. The game ends when someone reaches 66 or more points; the player with the fewest total points wins.',
    Player: 'Each turn all players simultaneously choose one card and reveal them together. Cards are placed in ascending order onto one of four table rows: each card goes on the row whose end card is lower than the played card and closest in value (smallest difference). If a card is the 6th on a row, the player takes the five existing cards as penalty (Horns) and their card starts a new row. If the played card is lower than all row ends, the player chooses a row to take and their card starts that row. After 10 turns the round ends; players sum their Horn points. The game ends when someone reaches 66 or more points; the player with the fewest total points wins.',
    objective: 'Score the fewest points (Horns) by the end of the game.',
    gameplay: 'Each turn all players simultaneously choose one card and reveal them together. Cards are placed in ascending order onto one of four table rows: each card goes on the row whose end card is lower than the played card and closest in value (smallest difference). If a card is the 6th on a row, the player takes the five existing cards as penalty (Horns) and their card starts a new row. If the played card is lower than all row ends, the player chooses a row to take and their card starts that row. After 10 turns the round ends; players sum their Horn points. The game ends when someone reaches 66 or more points; the player with the fewest total points wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Play one card per turn simultaneously; cards resolved from lowest to highest.',
      'Place card on the row where the end card is lower than your card and closest in value.',
      'Placing the 6th card on a row: take the five cards as penalty (Horns), your card starts the row.',
      'If your card is lower than all four row ends, choose a row to take; your card starts that row.',
      'Game ends when a player reaches 66 or more total Horn points; lowest total wins.',
